            <ArticleTitle>Chyloabdomen in a mature cat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mature, castrated male cat presented with progressive lethargy and a severely distended abdomen. Abdominal radiographs, abdominocentesis, and evaluation of the fluid obtained led to a diagnosis of chyloabdomen. The underlying pathology, etiology, diagnosis, and treatment associated with this disease are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
